"""The inventory of the static census (C23.6-3, C23.9-11; SG): every (file, function) of bayesreg/, experiments/, scripts/ and runs/ that holds a reading primitive or
builds the path of a subject's file (tests/test_bayesreg/sg/_census.py), with its class.  G: the subjects pass a general guard (load_pair, check_pair_subjects,
check_subject_admitted, ...); L: the tool's own second lock (eval.truth, HE sealed_admission, eval_seg.admit_subjects, LabelGuard, a4_admission, pinned pair lists);
F: a development stage or list written in the code (F_STAGES; disjointness tested); S: synthetic data only; D: reads a derived artefact by path, or no subject file
(git, systemctl, nvidia-smi, dmesg, record strings); P: a low-level reader changed by SG to pass C23.4-2 (or its step 3) itself; E: the hold-out evaluation entry of
C23.12 (bayesreg/eval/holdout.py only: its reader read_truth / _load_label_volume, the pair evaluation that calls it and the constants they use; EV, 11-07);
R: runs/ one-off scripts of finished runs and the two generators exempted by C23.2-2; T (LP-C2, contract C26.5-12, D147): the LPBA40 evaluation entry of C26.7
(bayesreg/eval/lpba_eval.py only: its label reader read_label / _label_volume, the pair evaluation that calls it and the constants they use).
Drafted by the implementer of SG (2026-11-07): the rows named in C23.6 are classified as the contract says; the rest by reading the call site, and where that rests on the
tool's other functions rather than on this one the note says 〔推断〕.  The reviewer checks the classes; a new or vanished row fails the census test until it is classified
and reviewed.
Convention of this package (kept by the lead's ruling, 2026-11-07 about 7:33 PM CST): the contract's classes have none for a match that reads no subject file at all --
a subprocess of git, systemctl, nvidia-smi or dmesg, a signal to a process group, a record string or a file-name constant; such rows are put in D with a note that says so.
Follow-up (SG code review I3, contract C23 revision 6h, 2026-11-07): the 70 rows of the generic subprocess note were re-read one by one.  A function that launches a
child which reads a subject's files (a systemd-run unit or a subprocess of a solver, worker or evaluator) is classed by the child's guard, not D: eta/sweep System.run,
spd/profile_native driver and tc/run_tc run_measure are G now; the other 67 only run git, systemctl, nvidia-smi, lscpu or a python version probe, and their note
no longer names systemd-run.  Read along the way, outside those 70: five D rows that call load_pair or launch an evaluator were reclassified (four G, one L)."""

